---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import TopicHubHero from '../../components/TopicHubHero.astro';

const title = 'Corporate Wellness Programs & Employee Fitness';
const description = 'Build a practical corporate wellness program with employee fitness, mobility, nutrition, recovery, ergonomics and mental performance support.';
const features = ['Employee fitness', 'Mobility', 'Nutrition', 'Hybrid teams'];
const faqs = [
  { question: 'What should a corporate wellness program include?', answer: 'A useful program can combine movement, strength, mobility, recovery, nutrition education, stress-management skills, ergonomics and organizational support. The right mix depends on employee needs, work demands, company size and available resources.' },
  { question: 'How do you make employees participate in workplace wellness?', answer: 'Participation improves when activities are convenient, inclusive, clearly communicated and supported by leadership. Offer short options at different ability levels, protect employee privacy and ask employees what would actually help them.' },
  { question: 'Can corporate fitness work for remote and hybrid teams?', answer: 'Yes. On-demand workouts, live virtual sessions, mobility breaks, educational resources and team challenges can reach employees across locations and schedules. Avoid making participation depend on access to a gym or being in one office.' },
  { question: 'How should employers measure a wellness program?', answer: 'Start with practical measures such as enrollment, repeat participation, completion, employee feedback and awareness while protecting individual health information.' }
];
const pageUrl = new URL('/corporate-wellness/', Astro.site).toString();
const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type':'WebPage', name:'Corporate Wellness Programs and Employee Fitness', description, url:pageUrl, dateModified:'2026-08-25' },
    { '@type':'FAQPage', mainEntity:faqs.map((item)=>({ '@type':'Question', name:item.question, acceptedAnswer:{ '@type':'Answer', text:item.answer } })) }
  ]
};
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/corporate-wellness/">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
  <TopicHubHero
    eyebrow="Corporate Wellness"
    heading="Wellness support built around your actual team."
    lead="Give employees practical movement, recovery, nutrition and wellness resources without turning work into a fitness competition."
    primaryLabel="Discuss a Corporate Program"
    primaryHref="/contact/"
    secondaryLabel="See the Program Framework"
    secondaryHref="#program-framework"
    {features}
    accent="teal"
    image="/images/app/screenshot-2.png"
    image2="/images/app/screenshot-4.png"
    visualTitle="One hub. Different starting points."
    visualText="Support office, remote, hybrid and active workforces with resources people can use on their own schedule."
  />

  <section class="section corp-overview">
    <div class="container corp-intro">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">What it can include</div><h2>More useful than another step challenge.</h2></div>
      <p>Corporate wellness works best when employees can quickly find something relevant to their needs, schedule and ability level. The program should be easy to enter, optional to use and broad enough to support more than the already-active employees.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="container corp-grid">
      <article class="corp-card"><span>01</span><h3>Movement &amp; strength</h3><p>Short workouts, beginner pathways and low-equipment options for different starting points.</p></article>
      <article class="corp-card"><span>02</span><h3>Mobility &amp; recovery</h3><p>Desk mobility, warmups, cooldowns and lower-intensity sessions people can use when they need them.</p></article>
      <article class="corp-card"><span>03</span><h3>Nutrition education</h3><p>Practical guidance around balanced meals, protein, hydration and recovery without restrictive challenges.</p></article>
      <article class="corp-card"><span>04</span><h3>Mental performance</h3><p>Breathing, awareness and reflection tools that support focus and consistency without replacing professional care.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt" id="program-framework">
    <div class="container framework-grid">
      <div class="framework-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow">Program framework</div>
        <h2>Start small. Learn what people use. Build from there.</h2>
        <p>A useful pilot does not need dozens of features. Give employees a clear starting point, make access simple and learn from repeat participation instead of launch-day enrollment alone.</p>
        <a class="btn" href="/corporate-wellness/employee-wellness-app/">Employee Wellness App Guide</a>
      </div>
      <div class="framework-steps">
        <div><b>01</b><span><strong>Assess</strong><small>Employee needs, schedules, locations and access barriers.</small></span></div>
        <div><b>02</b><span><strong>Choose</strong><small>A small set of goals and an inclusive starting pathway.</small></span></div>
        <div><b>03</b><span><strong>Launch</strong><small>One clear home for movement and wellness resources.</small></span></div>
        <div><b>04</b><span><strong>Refine</strong><small>Use participation and feedback to simplify the next version.</small></span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section workforce-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">Different workforces</div><h2>The program should fit the work.</h2></div>
      <div class="grid three">
        <a class="card" href="/workplace-wellness/"><span class="pill">Office</span><h3>Desk-based teams</h3><p>Movement breaks, ergonomics, mobility and practical strength support around long periods of sitting.</p></a>
        <article class="card"><span class="pill">Distributed</span><h3>Remote &amp; hybrid</h3><p>On-demand sessions and minimal-equipment options that do not depend on headquarters or one schedule.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span class="pill">Active work</span><h3>Field &amp; shift teams</h3><p>Recovery, hydration and movement support that recognizes physically demanding work is different from recreational exercise.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container resource-grid">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Go deeper</div><h2>Corporate wellness resources.</h2></div>
      <div class="resource-links">
        <a href="/corporate-wellness/employee-wellness-app/"><strong>Employee Wellness App Guide</strong><span>What employers should compare before choosing a platform. →</span></a>
        <a href="/corporate-wellness/wellness-challenges-for-employees/"><strong>Wellness Challenges for Employees</strong><span>Inclusive challenge ideas beyond generic step contests. →</span></a>
        <a href="/corporate-wellness/san-diego/"><strong>Corporate Wellness in San Diego</strong><span>Ideas for local and distributed San Diego workforces. →</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq-wrap" id="questions">
    <div class="container faq-grid">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Quick answers</div><h2>Common questions.</h2></div>
      <div>{faqs.map((item)=><details class="faq-item"><summary>{item.question}<span>+</span></summary><p>{item.answer}</p></details>)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="corp-cta"><div class="container corp-cta-inner"><div><span>Everyone’s an Athlete for organizations</span><h2>Build around the people you actually employ.</h2></div><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Discuss Corporate Wellness</a></div></section>

  <style>
    .corp-overview{background:#fff}.corp-intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .85fr;gap:48px;align-items:end;margin-bottom:34px}.corp-intro h2,.framework-copy h2,.section-heading h2,.resource-grid h2,.faq-grid h2{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,4vw,3.7rem);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin:8px 0 0}.corp-intro>p{color:var(--muted);margin:0}.corp-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:12px}.corp-card{min-height:260px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:24px;padding:24px;background:#f7faf8;display:flex;flex-direction:column}.corp-card span{color:var(--teal-dark);font-size:.72rem;font-weight:850;letter-spacing:.1em}.corp-card h3{font-size:1.4rem;line-height:1.05;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:auto 0 9px}.corp-card p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.92rem;margin:0}.framework-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.85fr 1.15fr;gap:64px;align-items:center}.framework-copy p{color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem}.framework-steps{display:grid;border-top:1px solid var(--line-strong)}.framework-steps>div{display:grid;grid-template-columns:48px 1fr;gap:16px;padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-strong)}.framework-steps b{color:var(--teal-dark);font-size:.74rem}.framework-steps span{display:grid;gap:3px}.framework-steps strong{font-size:1.1rem}.framework-steps small{color:var(--muted);font-size:.9rem}.workforce-section{background:#fff}.section-heading{margin-bottom:28px}.resource-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.7fr 1.3fr;gap:54px}.resource-links{display:grid;border-top:1px solid var(--line-strong)}.resource-links a{padding:20px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line-strong);display:grid;gap:4px}.resource-links strong{font-size:1.15rem}.resource-links span{color:var(--muted)}.faq-wrap{background:#fff}.faq-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.65fr 1.35fr;gap:54px}.faq-item summary{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px}.corp-cta{background:#102022;color:#fff;padding:72px 0}.corp-cta-inner{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:40px}.corp-cta span{color:#8ee0d5;font-size:.78rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em}.corp-cta h2{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.8rem);line-height:.95;letter-spacing:-.06em;max-width:720px;margin:10px 0 0}.corp-cta .btn{background:#fff;color:#102022;border-color:#fff;box-shadow:none}@media(max-width:900px){.corp-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}.corp-intro,.framework-grid,.resource-grid,.faq-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.corp-cta-inner{display:grid}}@media(max-width:620px){.corp-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.corp-card{min-height:190px}.corp-cta{padding:54px 0}.corp-cta .btn{width:100%}}
  </style>
</BaseLayout>